Let $g(x,y) = f^2(x,y) = x^2 (1 - y^2) + 2xy\sqrt{(1 - x^2)(1 - y^2)} + y^2 (1 - x^2)$.
Then
\begin{align*}
\frac{\partial g}{\partial x} &= 2x(1 - y^2) + 2y\sqrt{(1 - x^2)(1 - y^2)} - 2x^3y\sqrt{\frac{1}{x^2}\cdot\frac{1}{y^2}} - 2xy^3\sqrt{\frac{1}{x^2}\cdot\frac{1}{y^2}}\\
&= 2x(1 - y^2) + 2y\sqrt{(1 - x^2)(1 - y^2)} - 4x^2y^2 \end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
\frac{\partial g}{\partial y} &= 2y(1 - x^2) + 2x\sqrt{(1 - y^2)(1 - x^2)} - 2xy^3\sqrt{\frac{1}{x^2}\cdot\frac{1}{y^2}} - 2x^3y\sqrt{\frac{1}{x^2}\cdot\frac{1}{y^2}}\\
&= 2y(1 - x^2) + 2x\sqrt{(1 - y^2)(1 - x^2)} - 4x^2y^2. \end{align*}
